  "reason": "The three completed experiments (config_016, config_048, config_011) all use scgpt + imagenet_vit_l, varying only aggregation and fusion. The best so far is config_016 (avgpool + weighted, acc=0.542), but the image encoder dimension (imagenet_vit_l vs resnet50) remains completely untested. Config_014 (scgpt + resnet50 + avgpool + weighted) isolates the image encoder as a single variable change from the current best, directly testing whether a CNN backbone (ResNet50) can match or beat the ViT-L encoder for cellular image features. This is the highest-uncertainty design choice left unexplored, and resolving it early with 6 experiments remaining will guide whether to invest further in ViT-based or CNN-based image encoders for the rest of the budget."
}

